OneiOS 5101: reach the OneiOSRadeonGL target (src/gallium/targets/oneios-gl, the copy of
userland/metal-amd/gl that its build.sh makes) when it is there and GLES is built.

The hook sits after the DRI target, not at the end of the file, so that it applies on the
pinned Mesa alone (the host test, the softpipe-only iOS build) and after the guest Mesa
stage's 0005 and the Metal layer's 5002, which both add to the end. The target is read after
every driver (softpipe, radeonsi) it links.

diff --git a/src/gallium/meson.build b/src/gallium/meson.build
index 67011f5..8a19afd 100644
--- a/src/gallium/meson.build
+++ b/src/gallium/meson.build
@@ -232,6 +232,11 @@ if with_dri
   subdir('frontends/dri')
   subdir('targets/dri')
 endif
+# OneiOS (userland/metal-amd/gl, 5101-oneios-gl-target.patch): OneiOSRadeonGL, the Galaxy A56's OpenGL ES for
+# CoreAnimation, where userland/metal-amd/gl/build.sh copied its sources in and GLES is built.
+if with_gles2 and fs.is_dir('targets/oneios-gl')
+  subdir('targets/oneios-gl')
+endif
 if with_platform_haiku
   subdir('frontends/hgl')
 endif
